        {
          "id": 2257849335,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Both cases are not common and probably there are not many protocols likely to do a one-octet retransmission (DNP3 seems to be one of them), so you had to choose.\n\nIf choosing _retransmission_ the 1st packet would still break the Object Export. The operator could ignore the packet as in the 1st case. Maybe it's better to let the operator decide what to do but it seems this freedom is not what was asked.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6797213,
            "username": "eugene.adell",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Eugène Adell",
            "state": "active",
